{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":27564,"name":"Olorunfemi Israel","username":"Raceey","avatar_template":"/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/r/e8c25b/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-11-18T20:19:08.434Z","cooked":"\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-27564-h-1-project-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27564-h-1-project-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e1. Project\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCKB ClearSign: a TypeScript library + CCC signer wrapper that independently verifies a transaction’s inputs and explains it in plain language before the user signs.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRepo: \u003ccode\u003egithub.com/RaceeyXo/ckb-clearsign\u003c/code\u003e (MIT)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-27564-h-2-applicant-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27564-h-2-applicant-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e2. Applicant\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRaceeyXo: software engineer (full-stack Web3, AI engineering). GitHub: \u003ccode\u003eRaceeyXo\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-27564-h-3-problem-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27564-h-3-problem-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e3. Problem\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA CKB transaction only references its inputs by out point (txHash:index). The capacity, lock, type and data of those cells come from an indexer/RPC, and CCC trusts that answer. A lying, compromised or MITM’d RPC can make a wallet show “fee 0.0001 CKB” while the user actually signs something very different. As discussed in the October DevRel AMA, CCC deliberately trusts its indexer, and this check belongs in the wallet.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRelated work: CellGuard (CKBuilder projects \u003cspan class=\"hashtag-raw\"\u003e#48\u003c/span\u003e) inspects transactions against policies but resolves inputs via RPC. Pocket Node decodes transactions in-wallet. CKB Contract Flow only decodes committed transactions. ClearSign is complementary: it \u003cem\u003eproves\u003c/em\u003e input cell data by re-hashing origin transactions and ships as a CCC signer wrapper that tools like these can sit on.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-27564-h-4-solution-v01-already-built-and-working-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27564-h-4-solution-v01-already-built-and-working-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e4. Solution (v0.1 already built and working)\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003everifyInputs:\u003c/strong\u003e fetches each input’s origin tx, re-hashes it locally (blake2b) and rejects any mismatch. RPC-supplied cell data is never trusted.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eexplainTransaction:\u003c/strong\u003e per-address CKB sent/received, xUDT movements, mint/burn, fee, and a list of type scripts it can’t explain (flagged, not guessed).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eClearSignSigner:\u003c/strong\u003e wraps any ccc.Signer (verify → explain → user confirm → sign) and checks the signed tx hash equals the confirmed one.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eHonest guarantees:\u003c/strong\u003e two separate flags. inputDataVerified = true; chainStateVerified = false in v0.1. It explains asset movements, not contract outcomes.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-27564-h-5-proof-it-works-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27564-h-5-proof-it-works-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e5. Proof it works\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTested on Windows and Linux: 39 offline tests on 5 recorded testnet transactions (2 xUDT), plus a live public-testnet check.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLying-RPC demo:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ePlain CCC + lying RPC accepts a forged input (288 CKB reported as 10,288 CKB).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eClearSign + honest RPC: verified and explained.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eClearSign + lying RPC: blocked with \u003ccode\u003eORIGIN_TX_HASH_MISMATCH\u003c/code\u003e before the user is asked anything.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003edApp pre-fills forged cell data: blocked with \u003ccode\u003ePREFILLED_CELL_OUTPUT_MISMATCH\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eReproduce:\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003ccode\u003egit clone github.com/RaceeyXo/ckb-clearsign\u003c/code\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003ccode\u003enpm install\u003c/code\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003ccode\u003enpm test\u003c/code\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003ccode\u003enpm run demo -- --offline\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e(Screenshots of the demo and test runs will be added once my forum account can post images.)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-27564-h-6-why-a-signer-wrapper-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27564-h-6-why-a-signer-wrapper-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e6. Why a signer wrapper\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA library used only by the dApp protects users from honest dApps. A malicious dApp just skips it. Real protection is in the signer/wallet, so ClearSign ships as a drop-in CCC signer wrapper, and this grant funds a pilot in a real wallet.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-27564-h-7-scope-to-do-6-weeks-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27564-h-7-scope-to-do-6-weeks-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e7. Scope \u0026amp; to-do (6 weeks)\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWk 1: Harden v0.1 (edge cases, cross-platform scripts, browser build), publish to npm.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWk 2: Docs + integration guide for wallet developers.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWk 3–4: Pilot integration in one CKB wallet (PR or fork + write-up).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWk 5: “Trusted node” mode (verifyClient) + prototype chain-state check, documented with its limits.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWk 6: Completion report on Nervos Talk: results, wallet feedback, next steps.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOut of scope: Spore/iCKB/DAO decoding, contract simulation.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-27564-h-8-budget-1000-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27564-h-8-budget-1000-8\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e8. Budget: $1,000\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eDevelopment \u0026amp; testing (wks 1, 3–5): $750\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eDocs \u0026amp; integration guide (wk 2): $150\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCompletion report \u0026amp; community support (wk 6): $100\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-27564-h-9-milestones-9\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27564-h-9-milestones-9\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e9. Milestones\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eM1 (wk 2): npm package v0.2 + docs\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eM2 (wk 4): working wallet pilot\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eM3 (wk 6): chain-state prototype + final report\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-11-28T05:42:07.475Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":7,"reads":26,"readers_count":25,"score":100.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":11259,"topic_slug":"spark-program-ckb-clearsign-verify-before-you-sign","display_username":"Olorunfemi Israel","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":3,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://talk.nervos.org/t/ckb-ecosystem-biweekly-update/9821/35","internal":true,"reflection":true,"title":"CKB Ecosystem Biweekly Update","clicks":1}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":2}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":4566,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/spark-program-ckb-clearsign-verify-b